| `shell.shebang_shells` | list of strings | `["sh", "bash"]` | a non-empty list of bare program names, with no whitespace or path separator | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.shebang_shells` row | Decides which interpreters are judged: a file with no script suffix is a shell script only when its `#!` line, after `env` and its options, names one of these. `dash`, `ksh`, `zsh` and any other shell are not judged by default; add the name to judge them, with a linter that reads that dialect. A `.jinja` file is a template's source and is never judged, whatever its first line. A malformed list is exit 14. Absent, the targets write `[using default] shell.shebang_shells = ["sh", "bash"]` to stderr. | suffixes: `shell.script_suffixes` | always |
